---
// Each feature is shown working: the recordings share one size so the rows line up.
const features = [
  {
    title: 'Install any Zig',
    body: [
      'Install a tagged release, the latest nightly with <code>master</code>, or the newest stable release with <code>stable</code>. Shorthand like <code>.15</code> resolves to the highest 0.15.x, and full development build identifiers work too.',
      'Add <code>--zls</code> and ZVM installs a matching Zig Language Server alongside it. Official archives are checked against Zig\'s Minisign key, and a failed download moves on to the next community mirror.',
    ],
    commands: [
      ['zvm i master --zls', 'Latest nightly, plus ZLS'],
      ['zvm i --skip-use 0.15.2', 'Install without switching to it'],
      ['zvm vmu zig mach', 'Pull future installs from Mach\'s version map'],
    ],
    more: ['/reference/install-zig/', 'Installing Zig'],
    video: 'home-install',
    label: 'zvm i master --zls downloads Zig master and a matching ZLS, verifies checksums and signatures, and installs both',
  },
  {
    title: 'Switch in one command',
    body: [
      '<code>zvm use</code> changes which installed Zig runs when you type <code>zig</code>. Ask for a version you don\'t have and it offers to install it first.',
      'Inside a project, <code>zvm use</code> with no version reads <code>.minimum_zig_version</code> from <code>build.zig.zon</code>. To try a version once without switching, use <code>zvm run</code>.',
    ],
    commands: [
      ['zvm use stable', 'Highest installed stable release'],
      ['zvm use local', 'A Zig you built and linked as local'],
      ['zvm run 0.14.1 build', 'One command with 0.14.1'],
    ],
    more: ['/reference/switch-versions/', 'Switching versions'],
    video: 'home-switch',
    label: 'zvm ls lists installed versions, then zvm use switches between Zig 0.14.1 and 0.15.2',
  },
  {
    title: 'One version per shell',
    body: [
      'Add one line to your shell\'s startup file and every terminal keeps its own Zig. New shells start on the global default, and <code>zvm use</code> changes only the shell you\'re in.',
      'With <code>--use-on-cd</code>, entering a project switches to the version it declares, either a <code>//! zvm-lock:</code> line in <code>build.zig</code> or <code>.minimum_zig_version</code> in <code>build.zig.zon</code>. If that version isn\'t installed, ZVM tells you how to install it rather than downloading anything.',
    ],
    commands: [
      ['eval "$(zvm env --shell bash --use-on-cd)"', 'Bash; Zsh, Fish, and PowerShell work too'],
      ['zvm use --global 0.15.2', 'Change the default for new shells'],
    ],
    more: ['/reference/shell-integration/', 'Setting up per-shell versions'],
    video: 'home-shell',
    label: 'after zvm env is set up, entering a project whose build.zig pins 0.14.1 switches the shell from 0.15.2 to 0.14.1',
  },
  {
    title: 'Use less disk',
    body: [
      'Zig releases share much of their standard library. <code>zvm dedupe</code> hard-links identical files into one store, so each is kept once. In this recording, ten installed versions drop from 3.1&nbsp;GiB to 2.2&nbsp;GiB.',
      'Files are shared only when their content, permissions, and owner match. It\'s safe to repeat or interrupt, and removing a version cleans up store files nothing else uses.',
    ],
    commands: [
      ['zvm dedupe --auto on', 'Deduplicate every future install'],
      ['zvm dedupe .15', 'Only the 0.15.x installs'],
    ],
    more: ['/reference/deduplicate-versions/', 'Deduplicating versions'],
    video: 'home-dedupe',
    label: 'zvm dedupe shares identical files across ten installed Zig versions and reclaims 924.7 MiB',
  },
];

---

<div class="home-features not-content">
  {features.map((f) => (
    <section class="feature">
      <div class="copy">
        <h3>{f.title}</h3>
        {f.body.map((para) => <p set:html={para} />)}
        <a class="more" href={f.more[0]}>{f.more[1]}</a>
      </div>
      <div class="demo">
        <figure class="terminal-demo">
          <video autoplay loop muted playsinline preload="metadata" width="1000" height="540" poster={`/videos/${f.video}.webp`} aria-label={`Terminal recording: ${f.label}`}>
            <source src={`/videos/${f.video}.webm`} type="video/webm" />
            <source src={`/videos/${f.video}.mp4`} type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
        </figure>
        <dl class="commands">
          {f.commands.map(([cmd, what]) => (
            <div>
              <dt><code>{cmd}</code></dt>
              <dd>{what}</dd>
            </div>
          ))}
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}
</div>

<style>
  .home-features {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .feature {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 19rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    align-items: start;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--sl-color-white);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .feature .terminal-demo {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .feature video {
    aspect-ratio: 1000 / 540;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--zvm-font-display);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  .copy p {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }

  .more {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* One shared grid so every description starts in the same column. */
  .commands {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem;
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .commands > div {
    display: contents;
  }

  .commands dt code {
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  .commands dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }

  .home-features .copy :global(code) {
    font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.88em;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .home-features :global(a) {
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .feature {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .commands {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      row-gap: 0.1rem;
    }

    .commands dd {
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
